rdering statements in doc.go and Ready.Messages need applicability resolution.'])\nb('b_snapshot','A3','raft follower','Snapshot committed index and ConfState','MsgSnap',['s_recovery','s_log_commit'],implementation_guards=['Ignore index at or below commit; require follower and recipient membership; matching log fast-forwards commit instead of restoring snapshot.'],writes=['Restore log committed boundary and unstable snapshot, reconstruct progress via confchange.Restore.'],cross_activity_effects={'A1':'Snapshot supplies committed history and reestablishes participating configuration.','A2':'Recovery restores membership used for future authority acquisition.'},unknowns=['confchange.Restore internals and storage restoration caller not yet traced.'])\nb('b_config','A4','raft configuration application','Applied configuration and current leader progress','switchToConfig',['s_config_commit','s_leader_admit'],writes=['Replace tracker configuration/progress and learner status.'],important_branches=['Removed or demoted leader optionally steps down and returns.','Remaining leader reevaluates commitment; advancing commit broadcasts append without the pending-read release call in MsgAppResp.'],cross_activity_effects={'A1':'Changing voter aggregation can advance commitment using existing progress.','A2':'Removal can terminate authority depending on stepDownOnRemoval.'},unknowns=['Legal producer histories for configuration-induced first current-term commit are not established.'])\nb('b_application','A5','RawNode and external application','Committed, applying, applied and stable boundaries','Ready production and completion',['s_log_apply','s_advance','s_usage'],implementation_guards=['Pending or in-progress snapshot blocks committed entry delivery.','Async mode caps applicable index at locally stable prefix; sync mode allows unstable entries under Ready caller ordering.'],external_effects=['Ready provides committed entries; accepting Ready marks applying, while completion response or Advance accounts application.'],unknowns=['Node event loop serialization and configuration application ordering need reading.'])\nroles=json.load(open('../research.json'))['activity_roles']\nacts=[]\nfor a,r in roles.items():\n ids=[x['id'] for x in beh if x['primary_activity']==a]\n acts.append(dict(class_id=a,applicability='applicable',purpose=r['relation'],realization_summary=('Partially traced through '+', '.join(ids)) if ids else 'Caller responsibilities include retries, persistence and ordered Ready consumption; client endpoint is outside the core library.',source_ids=['s_usage'],unknowns=['Detailed boundary and alternate paths remain open.']))\nmapobj=dict(version=1,target_profile=dict(system_boundary='Captured Go raft library, RawNode/Node interfaces, log and progress machinery; callers supply persistence, transport and application execution.',protocol_contexts=['Per-node term, role, log, progress tracker and configuration','Synchronous Ready/Advance and asynchronous storage messages'],source_ids=['s_usage','s_async','s_ready']),activities=acts,behaviors=beh,facts=[],surfaces=[dict(entry_point='doc.go Ready processing versus Ready.Messages',disposition='UNCLASSIFIED_PROTOCOL_RESPONSIBILITY',reason='Usage permits sending messages during same-batch entry persistence, while Ready.Messages requires entry persistence first. Dependent append acknowledgments share Messages in sync mode; determine authoritative caller requirement before any experiment.',source_ids=['s_usage','s_ready_contract','s_ready'],high_consequence=True),dict(entry_point='raft.switchToConfig pending reads',disposition='mapped',behavior_ids=['b_config','b_ack_commit'],reason='Both paths may advance commit, but only append-response path calls releasePendingReadIndexMessages. Need legal first-current-term-commit history and read completion contract.',source_ids=['s_config_commit','s_ack_commit','s_release_reads'])],core_overview=dict(status='incomplete',formation=dict(explanation='Leader appends proposals with term and index and queues its own persistence-dependent acknowledgment. Follower verifies log prefix, appends a nonconflicting suffix and queues an acknowledgment. Leader consumes successful progress, asks tracker for committed candidate, and commits only a matching current-term entry. Commit updates propagate by append; committed entries are delivered through Ready with snapshot and local stability restrictions.',behavior_ids=['b_ack_commit','b_append_accept','b_persist_response','b_application'],source_ids=['s_reset_append','s_ack_commit','s_recovery','s_log_commit','s_log_apply']),context=dict(explanation='Campaign changes role and normally increments term; self-vote waits for persistence. Candidate polls responses of the matching election type and becomes leader on VoteWon. Higher-term messages normally step down; pre-vote has explicit exceptions. Reset clears progress and readOnly tracking; obsolete messages are filtered, with explicit snapshot completion handling for stale local append responses.',behavior_ids=['b_authority','b_persist_response'],source_ids=['s_campaign_step','s_authority','s_dispatch']),connection=dict(explanation='Term filtering, reset of progress and the current-term commit condition connect eligible support to authority. Durable log and committed snapshot state survive role transitions while transient vote and progress accounting resets. Configuration installation replaces aggregation context and can itself advance commitment. Ready separates delivery from storage and application completion.',behavior_ids=['b_authority','b_ack_commit','b_snapshot','b_config','b_application'],source_ids=['s_reset_append','s_campaign_step','s_config_commit','s_advance']),core_gaps=['Read tracker quorum aggregation, configuration changer and callers to establish qualification through membership transitions.','Trace initialization from persistent state, campaign admission/timers, and Node dispatch/Ready completion.','Finish pending reads and leader-transfer lifecycle to explain handling of old requests across authority transitions.'],open_details=['Same-batch persistence contract discrepancy.','Configuration-induced commit versus deferred read release.'],rationale='First partial backbone captures actual read paths and sourced discrepancies without declaring readiness or fabricating a formal Fact.'))\njson.dump(mapobj,open('map.json','w'),indent=2)\nsub=dict(action='research',rationale='Preserve the first sourced partial core map and two unresolved boundaries before completing membership, reconstruction and pending-work tracing.',sources=sources,map_path='map.json',feedback=dict(ref_ids=['b_authority','b_persist_response','b_config','s_storage_resp','s_config_commit','s_ready_contract'],answered='Read source ties support durability to msgsAfterAppend and ordered storage completion, not merely volatile log presence. Storage response term guards prevent stale entry stabilization while snapshot completion survives term changes. Configuration installation may advance commit but does not share the append-response pending-read release effect. No defect or formal obligation is asserted.',remaining=mapobj['core_overview']['core_gaps']+mapobj['core_overview']['open_details'],understanding='updated',rationale='These are source observations and specific unresolved premises; the map remains incomplete and no execution evidence is claimed.'))\njson.dump(sub,open('submission.json','w'),indent=2)\nPY\npython3 build_submission.py\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-03_11-17-23-etcd_raft-real-run --submission submission.json\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
